From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/imagination: carry the mainline driver instead of 6.18.36's

The code is mainline's (Imagination Technologies and the drm/imagination
contributors, see the mainline history of drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/); this
patch only carries it.

Replaces drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/ wholesale with the current mainline
directory (79 files; mainline 551c722f4080, v7.3-rc5-37, read 2026-09-30).
60 commits were ahead of what 6.18.36 ships at the read of 2026-09-08; three
more have merged since:

    7b824c293a6b drm/imagination: Propagate map failures correctly from
                 pvr_mmu_map_sgl()
    0a8224058a58 drm/imagination: Fix page count for page table for map()
                 interface (Cc stable: the page-table demand was computed
                 without the GPU VA, so map() fails at page-table boundaries)
    45585c3aa285 drm/imagination: clamp freelist reconstruction requests

They touch pvr_free_list.c, pvr_mmu.c, pvr_mmu.h and pvr_vm.c and nothing
else; include/uapi/drm/pvr_drm.h is byte-identical to 6.18.54's, and no
commit to it has merged since the read of 2026-09-08. Nothing else merged to
drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/ in that window.

Regenerated against 6.18.53 (3-way rebase). Stable 6.18.42 and 6.18.53
backported eight of the mainline commits this directory already carries
(6253bb56bb2e, c45fafa69fe3, b983a35dad37, c88fdbf3da26, e2c29d51c0f6,
943fa73ea0ef, 6d40846b8aa3, 2d607646909a), so that diff shrank to 2952 lines
over 42 files. The one conflict, pvr_queue.c, resolved to the carry copy: it
holds every line stable adds to pvr_queue.c between 6.18.36 and 6.18.53,
except one comment that mainline itself rewrote later.

Regenerated on 2026-09-30 against 6.18.54 with the three commits above: the
directory is now the mainline one byte for byte, and the diff is 3070 lines
over 43 files (pvr_mmu.h joins the set; the rest of the change is the three
commits). The kernel-side shims (`kernel-compat-shims-for-the-mainline-powervr-driver`) did not change.

WHY THE WHOLE DRIVER AND NOT A HANDFUL OF FIXES. Seven were carried first
and that was the wrong size of answer. This project's earlier Armbian-based port
of this board had already found the gaps in this driver, and the driver
states them itself -- in the tree we were shipping:

    /* @FIXME - hardcoding of numbers here is intended as an intermediate step
     * so the UAPI can be fixed, but requires a refactor in the future to store
     * them in a more appropriate location */
    static const u32 umd_quirks_musthave[] = { 47217, 49927, ...

pvr_drv.c says that twice, for quirks and for enhancements, and pvr_fw.c:388
marks the counter-dump path "Currently unsupported". Those are not defects to
be patched around one at a time; they are an unfinished driver saying so, and
upstream has since done the work -- pvr_check.h, the reordered
pvr_device_features, the BXM-4-64 MC1 promotion, "Warn or error on unsupported
hardware", the gpuid parameter and its KUnit test.

WHAT ARRIVES THAT WE DID NOT HAVE. Beyond the seven already carried: context
reset notification handling and the missing rogue reset reasons -- the recovery
path that was never seen running on this board -- "Don't timeout job if its
fence has been signaled", the FW-initialised state accessors, the power-off and
suspend-path fixes, and TRACE POINTS. That last one is not a nicety here: the
main obstacle in investigating the load hang was that it could not see what the
GPU was doing.

WHAT IT COSTS, measured rather than asserted. Three things mainline uses do not
exist here in the expected form, and all three are handled in `kernel-compat-shims-for-the-mainline-powervr-driver`, which is a
separate patch precisely so this one stays a clean import: an optional GFP
argument in slab.h, a pwrseq rename, and a 26-line drm_gpuvm function built on
primitives already present. An earlier estimate framed that cost as "core
kernel surgery in three subsystems" -- wrong, and corrected by measuring it.
`kernel-compat-shims-for-the-mainline-powervr-driver` carries the honest version, including which of its hunks is actually
risky.

⚠ WHAT THIS IS NOT. It is not proven better than what it replaces, and it
cannot be yet: both drivers pass every test this tree can run today, because the
load hang has never been reproduced here. It is not a fix for that hang. And it
is a 3070-line diff over 43 files -- reviewable as an import, not as a change
set, which is the honest way to read it.

⚠ AND OUR SERIES NOW DEPENDS ON IT. The seven fixes carried before (six of
these commits plus one from mainline) are redundant by construction with the
full driver in place and are dropped in the same series. Keeping both would mean
applying the same change twice.

VERIFIED: applies at --fuzz=0 (whole series, the apply-patches build stage),
compile-check green with
drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/ added to the gate -- and that gate extension is not
optional here, because without it the cheap gate does not compile this driver at
all. ⚠ NOT hardware-proven.

Assisted-by: Claude
